,14,1,"chatted about this later; this isn't quite right, since the listeners for an extension are removed async from its unload. This means that in the case of an extension update, it's possible the new…"],["d5afa127_a2faa805",27,14,0,"Not from this CL, but it looks like a [subsequent CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7166297) added security info listener tracking, which I think we'll need to update…"],["f32f9a72_db5f7157",22,14,1,"nit: could just use brace initialization for this since there's a ctor that takes a single feature to be enabled"]],0,288],[7165414,20412,42,1.326,1.047,[[4,0.667,44,29],[6,0.244,16,10],[5,0.089,6,3]],[["7f031c88_7ac47443",22,14,1,"this seems like it could _potentially_ be racy, since we do this after waiting for the blank page to load in a new OTR browser. Maybe put these before that part (around line 2878), grabbing the…"],["b6375a11_8118da07",22,14,0,"this is probably worth chatting about; we don't usually want to persist data from OTR contexts (but this is fine for now)"]],0,289],[7188066,20416,5,0.242,0.169,[[27,0]],[],0,290],[7208362,20419,2,0.467,0.267,[[14,13]],[],0,291],[7210258,20423,3,0.25,0.212,[[6,17]],[],0,292],[7206262,20423,58,1.21,0.931,[[28,0.95,5,56],[29,0.05,2,2]],[],0,293],[7213237,20423,14,0.295,0.242,[[6,18]],[["54a5a7ee_c0f3329f",27,0,0,"optional: *maybe* cleaner with a find_if() != end()?"]],0,294],[7204299,20426,60,1.197,0.975,[[1,36]],[],0,295],[7146923,20426,27,0.675,0.504,[[0,20]],[["14b81d7d_2710839e",18,0,1,"nit: \\`backticks\\` in new code (even though this is just moved) optional nit: Could/should these be inline constexpr char?"]],0,296],[7233758,20427,18,0.675,0.504,[[0,21]],[],0,297],[7233757,20430,7,0.248,0.178,[[30,73]],[],0,297],[7233314,20430,3,0.25,0.212,[[6,19]],[],0,298],[7227604,20430,81,2.194,1.837,[[6,0.765,20,62],[4,0.235,45,19]],[["02163b22_972d53da",29,-2,1,"nit: InitFromInactiveListenerValue() or just FromInactiveListenerValue()?"],["3b561591_5acd4c0a",27,-2,1,"